      "description": "THE headline view: fleet inference pressure (60s window) split into two stacked bands. The stack HEIGHT is total inference-full (fraction of the window every active worker was blocked on inference at once); the COLOR split shows how much of that was PRODUCTIVE (green — generating tokens, compute-bound) versus STALLED (red — blocked but not generating: 429 back-off / network / TTFT / queueing, i.e. rate-limit bound). When the red band dominates a tall stack, more parallelism buys nothing. productive = full − stalled, clamped at 0. Main loop excluded."
